item.description:
Listen to audiobook in full for free : <br><a href="https://amzn.to/4hopIfn">https://amzn.to/4hopIfn</a> <br><br>Title: Prophet<br>Author: Kahlil  Gibran<br>Narrator: Petr Filin<br>Length: 2:07:57<br>Release date: 06-17-2025<br>Publisher: Authors Republic<br>Genres: Non-Fiction, Philosophy<br>Language: English<br><br>Description:<br>One of the world’s most beloved spiritual classics – The Prophet has sold millions of copies and continues to inspire across generations.
In this lyrical collection of 26 prose poems, Kahlil Gibran gives voice to Almustafa, a prophet who shares his insights on love, work, freedom, joy, sorrow, and more as he prepares to leave the city he has lived in for twelve years. His words are simple yet profound – poetic yet universally accessible.
Blending Eastern mysticism with Western literary elegance, The Prophet offers timeless wisdom for every stage of life. Its reflections are ideal for moments of contemplation, celebration, grief, or spiritual seeking.
After listening to this book, you will learn:
• how to reflect more deeply on life’s essential experiences;
• the nature of unconditional love, and how to live it fully;
• why sorrow and joy are inseparable parts of the human journey;
• the meaning of work, freedom, and giving in a purposeful life;
• how to embrace your own spiritual path with grace and openness.
The Prophet is a poetic companion for the soul – gentle, profound, and endlessly inspiring.<br><br>#ad Disclosure: As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.

